\name{cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_rename}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_rename}
\title{Rename a camera path keyframe}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_rename(viewer, keyframe, label)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{keyframe}{A keyframe, by its label as the Camera path list shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{label}{The new label: the shot's name, and its caption while the path plays with captions on. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Give a keyframe another label, unique among the keyframes.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.keyframe.rename} (Camera path). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{camera-path}.
}
\seealso{
